#: ../chapter6.rst:59
msgid "Settings Explained"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:61
msgid "There are many settings under the Settings Manager in the desktop client. To access them click the Settings tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:66
msgid "SETTINGS TAB - SETTINGS MANAGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:70
msgid "Sync Throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:72
msgid "False (default) - If true, the Upload and Download Throttling control defined under this settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:75
msgid "Sync Throttled Upload Bandwidth (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:77
#: ../chapter6.rst:82
msgid "0 (default) - The default setting is unlimited KB/s, enter a number here to reduce the bandwidth consummed to the set limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:80
msgid "Sync Throttled Download Bandwidth (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:85
msgid "Full Speed Sync Stop Hour (default 7:00)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:87
msgid "7 (default) - This setting represents the hour (24 hour clock) of the day when Full Speed synchronization will stop - Usually it is desired to have full speed synchronization overnight when the Internet utilization is low."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:90
msgid "Full Speed Sync Start Hour (default 20:00)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:92
msgid "20 (default) - This setting represents the hour (24 hour clock) of the day when Full Speed synchronization will begin - Usually it is desired to have full speed synchronization overnight when the Internet utilization is low."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:95
msgid "Scan local files and sync-up to cloud as necessary"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:97
msgid "False (default) - The desktop client builds up a state database that describes which files are in sync and which files are not. In the case where the desktop client is re-imaged, the state information may be lost. This option can be used to scan local files and upload them to the cloud as necessary. This is a quick way to re-build state information when the local files are more accurate than the information in the cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:100
msgid "Scan cloud files and sync-down to local as necessary"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:102
msgid "False (default) - The desktop client builds up a state database that describes which files are in sync and which files are not. In the case where the desktop client is re-imaged, the state information may be lost. This option can be used to scan local files and upload them to the cloud as necessary. This is a quick way to re-build state information when the cloud files are more accurate than the local files."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:105
msgid "Allow shortcuts to sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:107
msgid "False (default) - By default, the Windows Client does not support file/folder shortcuts, as we cannot guarantee that the shortcuts in the cloud are always valid. If a user creates a shortcut from a computer and links to a local file. The shortcut is then uploaded to the cloud. If the user accesses the Windows Client from another computer, the shortcut will not work unless both computers have exactly the same files and folder structures. If the shortcut is broken, Windows Explorer will aggressively try to resolve the broken shortcut paths, which will slow down the Windows Client. If users only access their cloud files from the same computer/device, they may still want to save their shortcuts to the cloud. In this case, you should enable the \"Allow shortcuts to sync\" setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:110
msgid "Disable file-change logs for dummy files (zero byte files)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:112
msgid "False (default) - When set to True, sync will ignore file change log for empty files."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:115
msgid "Scheduled Sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:118
msgid "Enable Scheduled Sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:120
msgid "False (default) - If true, the synchronization and transferring of files will follow the schedule defined in this section."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:123
msgid "Pause Sync Start Hour (default 7:00)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:125
msgid "7 (default) - This setting represents the hour (24-hour clock) of the day when synchronization will pause."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:128
msgid "Pause Sync End Hour (default 20:00)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:130
msgid "20 (default) - This setting represents the hour (24-hour clock) of the day when synchronization will start."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:133
msgid "Mapped Drive Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:136
msgid "Always allow PDF preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:138
msgid "False (default) - If true, always allow windows client to show PDF file preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:141
msgid "Do not show storage quota"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:143
msgid "False (default) - If true, do not show the user's storage quota on windows client drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:146
msgid "When starting up the client, open the mounted drive automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:148
msgid "True (default) - When starting up the client, automatically open File Explorer to show the windows client drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:151
msgid "Cloud drive label"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:153
msgid "My Cloud Drive (default) - This is the drive label you can see from the Windows Explorer."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:156
msgid "Drive Letter"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:158
msgid "M (default) - This is the drive letter assignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:161
msgid "In offline-mode, only show files that are cached and available locally"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:163
msgid "False (default) - If true, when working in offline mode, only show files that are already in cache. Hide any files are not in cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:166
msgid "Disable \"check-out\" on files and folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:168
msgid "False (default) - If true, disable manual file lock/unlock."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:171
msgid "Use Windows' default browser to open files and folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:173
msgid "False (default) - If true, on windows client drive, when right click file/folder and select Open in Web Browser, open default browser to show the selected files."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:176
msgid "Always sync folder meta-data when browsing with Windows Explorer"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:178
msgid "False (default) - If true, when visiting cloud folder in windows client drive, the client will ignore local folder listing cahe. It will always get latest folder listing cache from cloud. It will generate high dir request to the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:181
msgid "Disable drive mounting"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:183
msgid "False (default) - If true, no Cloud Drive will be mounted under My Computer for the Windows Client."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:186
msgid "Create cloud drive shortcut under My Documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:188
msgid "True (default) - If true, there is a shortcut to the Cloud Drive under the My Documents' folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:191
msgid "Large File Upload"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:194
msgid "Enable \"chunking\" when uploading files larger than a specific size (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:196
msgid "15 (default) - When uploading large file, the client can split the file in small chunks and upload small chunks in parallel. It can improve the upload speed. Also if a chunk fails, only need to retry the chunk. This setting defines how large the file size is to enable the chunk feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:199
msgid "Default file chunk unit size (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:201
msgid "20 (default) - This setting defines the chunk size."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:204
msgid "Bandwidth Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:207
msgid "Download Bandwidth Limit (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:209
msgid "0 (default) - This setting is defaulted to unlimited. Change this to limit your download bandwidth to the number you enter in Kilobytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:212
msgid "Upload Bandwidth Limit (KB/s, 0-Unlimited)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:214
msgid "0 (default) - This setting is defaulted to unlimited. Change this to limit your upload bandwidth to the number you enter in Kilobytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:217
msgid "Maximum number of file transfert threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:219
msgid "5 (default) - Use this setting to restrict the number of threads used during synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:222
msgid "Local Cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:225
msgid "Cache Directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:227
msgid "C:\\\\Users\\\\username\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\gteamclient\\\\cache (default) - Use this setting to change the default location of the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:230
msgid "Cache Size Limit (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:232
msgid "0 (default) - The default setting is zero which is unlimited. Set this to a different number to limit the cache to that size in MB. You can disable the cache (not recommended) using the Web Portal's Tenant Dashboard > Roles settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:235
msgid "Minimum free disk space (GB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:237
msgid "5 (default) - The cache will leave defined free disk space on the disk. This can prevent the cached files use the entire disk. If zero, the cache can take entire disk space."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:240
msgid "Outlook Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:243
msgid "Prompt for conversion when a file is larger than a specific size (KB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:245
msgid "0 (default) - Default to never prompt. This setting defines how large the attachment file size is to use the Outlook plugin to automatically upload the file to Centrestack cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:248
msgid "Attachments cache folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:250
msgid "Outlook plugin will upload file to the defined folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:253
msgid "Link expiration time"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:255
msgid "Never (default) - When attaching a file to an Outlook email, the Windows Client can upload the file to the cloud and generate a link to access the file. The link is added in the email, to reduce email size. This setting defines how long the link will expire."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:258
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:261
msgid "Disable offline-mode notification"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:263
msgid "False (default) - A system that goes into offline mode will send a notification by default. Change this to True to hide that notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:266
msgid "Disable File-change notification"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:268
msgid "False (default) - When files are modified by other people or by the same user but from another machine, there is a file change notification. Change this setting to True to turn off that notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:271
msgid "Disable large file-download tracker window"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:273
msgid "False (default) - When Windows Explorer is downloading a large file in the background, by default there is a large file download progress dialog showing. This setting allows you to turn off that notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:276
msgid "Disable automatic task tracker for scheduled tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:278
msgid "False (default) - By default, there is an automatic task tracker for scheduled tasks. This setting allows you to turn off the tracker."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:281
msgid "Disable in-place-editing and preview-disabled notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:283
msgid "False (default) - When in-place-editing zip/exe file and preview-disabled, by default, the system will send a notification. This setting allows you to turn off that notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:286
msgid "Disable shut-down confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:288
msgid "False (default) - When shutdown the desktop client, there is a shutdown confirmation window. This setting controls whether that confirmation dialog will be shown. Set this to True to hide the confirmation dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:291
msgid "Disable folder move confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:293
msgid "False (default) - When moving a folder within windows client drive, by default, the system will show a confirmation dialog. This setting allows you to turn off that confirmation dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:296
msgid "Advanced Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:299
msgid "Enable in-place opening of zip and exe files"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:301
msgid "False (default) - By default, Windows Client doesn't allow a user to open zip files in mounted M drive directly. This is because opening a zip file means to download the whole zip file to cache first. When the zip file is big, the download will generate high network traffic and cause windows explorer to slow down. Change this to True if you want users to be able to open Zip files within the M drive. The next setting determines the size limit of this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:304
msgid "Max size of zip files allowed to open in-place (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:306
msgid "20 (default) - This defines the size limit for the zip file the user is allowed to open. It is designed to prevent user/windows explorer from downloading very large zip files. By default, it is 20M. When admin enables inplace zip file opening, only files within 20M can be opened."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:309
msgid "Max size of files for thumbnail generation (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:311
msgid "0 (default) - This defines the file size limit for generating thumbnail."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:314
msgid "Always allow picture previews"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:316
msgid "False (default) - If this is turned on preview thumbnails will be generated for your local files. This consumes a lot of bandwidth for unnecessary downloading of image files."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:319
msgid "Enable slow network mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:321
msgid "False (default) - No further information."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:324
msgid "Prevent computer from falling asleep during sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:326
msgid "True (default) - Nighttime is typically a good time to transfer files at full speed. However, the machine may go into a sleeping state, preventing the transfer of files. This setting can prevent the sleep mode from activating."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:329
msgid "Mount drive in global space"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:331
msgid "False (default) - No furter information."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:334
msgid "Upload hidden files"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:336
msgid "False (default) - Change this setting to True if you want to upload Hidden Files to the cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:339
msgid "Upload system files"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:341
msgid "False (default) - Change this setting to True if you want to upload System Files to the cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:344
msgid "Use Volume Shadow-Copy to upload files that are constantly accessed"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:346
msgid "False (default) - By default an actively opened file will not be uploaded until it has been closed. This setting can override that behavior, uploading all of the files regardless of their open status."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:349
msgid "Disable AutoCAD optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:351
msgid "False (default) - By default, windows client will delay the sync of AutoCAD files by combining several changes into a single change. This is specific for users who save frequently or have the AutoCAD autosave feature enabled with short intervals. The file change will not be uploaded to the cloud immediately after the file saving. Leave it Uncheck if only one person is working on the AutoCAD files. When the setting is checked, windows client will sync the file to cloud as soon as the file is saved. Check the setting if the user needs the change to be uploaded to cloud as soon as possible. When multiple users are working on same set of AutoCAD files, check the setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:354
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:357
msgid "Days of audit trace to keep"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:359
msgid "5 (default) - This setting defines how many days to keep the audit trace."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:362
msgid "Trace Level (0-Disable, 1-error, 2-warning, 3-info, 100-verbose)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:364
msgid "0 (default) - By default, the trace level is 0. It can be changed to the levels shown, or 101 for maximum debug trace."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:368
msgid "Sync Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:371
msgid "Task Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:373
msgid "Click on the Task Manager icon on top right corner of client menu to open Task Manager. You can see the summary for all the sync tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:378
msgid "TASK MANAGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:382
msgid "Client Side Management Console - Web Portal"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:384
msgid "Click the system tray icon (1) open the tray menu. From the three-dots (2) you can access other functions. By choosing \"Web Portal\" (3), the Windows client web portal will be opened in a default web browser. Click \"Management Console\" icon (4) to access management console from web."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:389
msgid "ACCESS MANAGEMENT CONSOLE WEB PORTAL"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:392
msgid "Device Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:394
msgid "Device Manager has an overview of the device including details such as Device Owner, Device Type, OS Type, Device Client Version (software build number), Last Login Time, Sync Status, Cache Size, Last Report Time, and more. Click \"Manage\" icon to see Device details."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:399
msgid "CLIENT MANAGEMENT CONSOLE - DEVICE MANAGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:405
msgid "Attached Folders are local folders that are maintaining a two-way synchronization relationship with cloud storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:410
msgid "ATTACHING A FOLDER TO THE CLOUD"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:413
msgid "Locked Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:415
msgid "A file that is in use is locked. In the image below, the user has opened the document **(1)** in Word. When a user is editing a Word Document, that file will remain locked while it is open in Word. Sometimes you will need to click the \"Refresh\" text **(2)** to see files that are locked in the Locked Files view. These are locked files from the local device. The locked files include automatically locked files (e.g., opened in Word) and manually locked files (e.g., right-clicked and locked in context menu). If you need to force-unlock a file, this can be done using the lock icon **(3)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter6.rst:420
msgid "LOCKED FILES VIEW"
msgstr ""

